{"nodes": [{"id": "context_architecture_invariant_1", "label": "Invariant 1: never str_replace over serialized data", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PHP serialization embeds byte lengths; a naive replace produces a value that can never be unserialized again. Proven in rewriter-test.php test 4."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_2", "label": "Invariant 2: unserialize with allowed_classes => false", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Blocks object injection, and refuses to write back a payload it cannot faithfully reconstruct when the result contains __PHP_Incomplete_Class."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_3", "label": "Invariant 3: use strtr(), not str_replace(), for the map", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "strtr applies the longest key first and never re-scans replaced text; ordering matters when one filename is a prefix-like fragment of another (photo.jpg vs photo-300x200.jpg)."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_4", "label": "Invariant 4: back up before the first destructive operation, roll back on any failure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Steps 2-9 of the convert pipeline are wrapped; a failure at any point restores from backup."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_5", "label": "Invariant 5: the Optimizer never touches the database or attachments", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It is shared by the upload path and the bulk path, which have completely different DB semantics."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_6", "label": "Invariant 6: never delete old files until after metadata regeneration succeeds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A failure mid-way must leave a working site."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_7", "label": "Invariant 7: estimate memory before decoding, only for in-process engines", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "width x height x 4 x 2 against memory_limit. The most common shared-host fatal, turned into a logged skip. Applying it to cwebp, which runs as a separate process, wrongly refused images it could handle."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_8", "label": "Invariant 8: soft errors are defined once, in AttachmentConverter::soft_errors()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PERMANENT_SKIPS plus RETRYABLE_SKIPS. This list was duplicated in three places and drifted, causing 496 skipped images to be reported as failures. Lets Scanner::requeue() return environment-caused skips to the queue without retrying unfixable images."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_9", "label": "Invariant 9: log status stays 'optimized' when a backup expires", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Availability is tracked by an empty backup_path instead. Changing the status would zero that image's contribution to the savings stats."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_10", "label": "Invariant 10: attachment references stored as IDs need no rewriting", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only hardcoded URL strings are touched. IDs resolve through metadata, which is updated separately; rewriting them would be wrong."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_11", "label": "Invariant 11: never rewrite derived caches, flush them instead", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "_elementor_css, _bricks_css*, _transient_*, _wp_attachment_metadata are regenerated from source data and their formats are not ours to edit."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_12", "label": "Invariant 12: build/ and vendor/ are committed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WordPress.org ships the plugin as-is; there is no npm or Composer step on the user's server. Edit resources/, never build/."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_13", "label": "Invariant 13: no external HTTP requests, ever", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Privacy claim in the readme, and a WordPress.org review requirement."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_14", "label": "Invariant 14: custom media-toolbar buttons must manage their own visibility", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Core's SelectModeToggle skips .media-button in both directions (media-grid.js:337,:350), so it never hides or re-shows them; a button that doesn't toggle its own hidden class gets stuck."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_15", "label": "Invariant 15: refetch the attachment model after converting it", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Conversion changes the filename. Without model.fetch() every thumbnail in the grid 404s and the modal shows stale data."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_16", "label": "Invariant 16: engine selection is a chain, not a choice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EngineFactory::chain() plus EngineInterface::supports_file(). An engine can read a format in general and still be wrong for one file (cwebp cannot rotate, GD cannot decode CMYK). An explicit preference moves an engine to the front, it does not replace the chain."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_17", "label": "Invariant 17: the logger writes to a file, never to the database", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It is called from inside the upload handler, cron and WP-CLI to record what happened while the rewriter was modifying the database. Errors are always written; only the verbose trail is gated on the setting."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_18", "label": "Invariant 18: cross-request locks use add_option(), not transients", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "get_transient() then set_transient() is check-then-set; two simultaneous requests both see 'unlocked'. The options table's unique key on option_name makes the database arbitrate. See Services\\Lock."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_19", "label": "Invariant 19: the rewriter invalidates only the objects it touched, never the whole cache", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Descriptors carry an object column and a cache group. wp_cache_flush() once per batch would discard a persistent object cache every few seconds during a bulk run, worst on the large sites that need bulk most."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_20", "label": "Invariant 20: old URLs resolve from an indexed table, matched on full path before basename", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "swift_image_optimizer_urls replaces a LIKE over a LONGTEXT column, which was unindexable and triggered by every bot probing an old filename. Basename-only matching also confused two images sharing a name in different month folders."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_21", "label": "Invariant 21: uploaded originals are backed up before the source is deleted", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gated on backup_uploads, failing closed. Without it an upload is a one-way door. The manifest is written in the same shape the converter path uses, so Restore needs no separate code path."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_22", "label": "Invariant 22: a column describing a file is not evidence the file exists \u2014 ask the disk", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "BackupManager::manifest_is_intact() before offering Restore, AttachmentConverter::optimized_output_exists() before reporting or refusing an optimization. The database and uploads directory can be restored from different points in time. Trusting the column showed a whole library as processed with no way to optimize any of it, and offered Restores that could not succeed. Three of Unit 11's four reports were this same mistake."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_23", "label": "Invariant 23: a batch persists its pending rewrite map before applying it", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runner parks pending_rewrite, rewrites, then clears it; the next batch flushes anything left behind. Conversion writes a terminal log row per image but repoints references once per batch; a death in between leaves those images marked done forever with references pointing at filenames that no longer exist, and Scanner never revisits a terminal row. Tolerable when a batch was one foreground request; not once cron runs batches unattended."}, {"id": "context_architecture_invariant_24", "label": "Invariant 24: the server owns whether a bulk run is active", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "start() is idempotent, cancel() keeps the cursor, and the client reconciles from state() rather than computing its own. Two clients doing their own arithmetic over different snapshots is why progress figures disagreed, and an unguarded start() let a second tab reset a run mid-flight, surfacing as 'already running' from a button that looked available."}, {"id": "context_architecture_backupmanager", "label": "BackupManager", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_attachmentconverter", "label": "AttachmentConverter", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_optimizer", "label": "Optimizer", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_scanner", "label": "Scanner", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_enginefactory", "label": "EngineFactory", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_engineinterface", "label": "EngineInterface", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_cwebpengine", "label": "CwebpEngine", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_logger", "label": "Logger", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_lock", "label": "Services\\Lock", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_databaserewriter", "label": "DatabaseRewriter", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_urllookup", "label": "UrlLookup / swift_image_optimizer_urls table", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_urlmap", "label": "UrlMap", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_runner", "label": "Services\\Bulk\\Runner", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_optimizationlog", "label": "OptimizationLog", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_databackfills", "label": "DataBackfills", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_dbmigrator", "label": "DBMigrator", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_architecture_storesettings", "label": "StoreSettings", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "context/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "sou